{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s35-p01",
      "text": "When a child first picked up a crayon, a line might have been the first mark he made.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p02",
      "text": "Then he learned to draw a straight line with the help of a ruler.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p03",
      "text": "He used lines to write numbers, symbols, and the letters of the alphabet.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p04",
      "text": "The lines on a map helped him find the best route from one place to another.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p05",
      "text": "He also used lines to draw pictures.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p06",
      "text": "Lines are everywhere.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p07",
      "text": "You can see lines in the grain of a piece of wood or in the cracks on a narrow sidewalk.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p08",
      "text": "You can see lines outside a building or in the field.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p09",
      "text": "Lines are also used to create art.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p10",
      "text": "In drawing, line is an element of art that is the path of a moving point through space.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p11",
      "text": "Artists use lines to lead your eyes through a work of art.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p12",
      "text": "A line can be drawn on paper with a pencil or scratched into wet clay with a stick.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p13",
      "text": "Depending on its direction, a line can express different ideas or feelings.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p14",
      "text": "Lines are used to express different images in Chinese calligraphic drawing.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p15",
      "text": "The word calligraphy means beautiful handwriting.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p16",
      "text": "In China, calligraphy is used to form characters that represent the language.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p17",
      "text": "Characters are more than just a letter of the alphabet.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p18",
      "text": "They can represent an idea, an object, or a verbal sound.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p19",
      "text": "Calligraphic lines are usually made with brush strokes that change from thin to thick in one stroke.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p20",
      "text": "To make a thin line, artists use the tip of the brush.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35-p21",
      "text": "As you press on the brush and more of it touches the paper, the line becomes wider.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p21.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
